# Sanghamitra — Sreenivas (owner) communications

## North star

Save **Sreenivas Garu**'s time. Make the site and admin easier for him — not more email, not builder noise, not duplicate messages to untangle.

Principal: **Pradeep Kotari** builds; **ainapura@yahoo.com** is the owner who fills admin and reviews the public site.

## External messages — hard stops

| User says | Meaning | Do NOT |
|-----------|---------|--------|
| **resend**, **review**, **draft** | Send **review to Pradeep only** (`pradeep.kotari@gmail.com`) | Send to `ainapura@yahoo.com` |
| **send** (or names Sreeni explicitly) | Send to **ainapura@yahoo.com**, Cc Pradeep | Assume consent from resend/review |
| **push** | Git commit + push only | Email anyone |

- Never send email, WhatsApp, or other external messages unless the principal explicitly approves the recipient.
- Prefer **one** clear letter over several same-subject emails the same day.
- Test mail to owner is forbidden (ISA A4); use Pradeep sign-in code path to prove mail.

## Address and voice

- Greeting: **Hi Sreenivas Garu** (not "Namaste Sreenivas" unless he prefers otherwise).
- Drafts **to** him: second person **you/your** throughout. Never "he/him" when explaining what the letter says to him.
- Pradeep signing: **Ask me to build something** — not "Ask Pradeep to build" in body copy.
- No builder jargon in owner-facing copy: D1, deploy, GitHub, Cloudflare, cache, admin tab, ISO timestamps, "goes live" without explaining **visitors see it within seconds; Pradeep gets a heads-up only**.

## What "save in admin" means (owner-facing explanation)

**A — On the website within seconds:** phone, homepage, donate, learn, enroll, sittings, uploads. He can use **View live site**. Pradeep gets informational email only.

**B — Not on the website until Pradeep builds:** Ask me to build something, What to build next.

**C — Visitor forms:** both get email; reply in login or WhatsApp; does not change public pages by itself.

WhatsApp remains the fastest door for day-to-day questions.

## Sign-in copy (consistent)

1. Enter **ainapura@yahoo.com**
2. Send the code
3. Check **Yahoo Mail** for the six-digit code — **use the latest one**
4. Sign in

## Product defaults for Sreeni

- Hide **Design choices** from owner; builder-only.
- Owner saves notify **Pradeep only**, not Sreeni.
- `/admin/#build-next` is the structured build menu; freeform notes stay under Ask me to build.
